                <pb facs="0417" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/178: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Spencer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-08T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Your October 1, 4 p.m., and Department’s October 4, 7 p.m. Department
                    understands that conferences similar to that suggested <pb facs="0418" n="320"
                        xml:id="pg320"/> have in the past been held at a point on the boundary near
                    Choluteca. If the opportunity presents itself, suggest discreetly to the
                    President that his conferences with President Chamorro be held there.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
